        "campaign_variables_tables": {
            "variable_key": {
                "lookup_hardcoded": "agents_per_tech_cap;;;;;The maximum number of agents that can be assigned to research one technology.:::::autoresolve_advantage_over_enemy_wipeout_threshold;;;;;(IN GAME) The advantage an alliance must have over the enemy, to wipe out the opposition on a win in the autoresolver:::::autoresolve_base_best_ship_kills_to_capture;;;;;(IN GAME) The base proportion of losing navy kills that should be converted to captures (may choose to not capture these depending on the random factor applied later):::::autoresolve_base_chance_a_unit_takes_captives;;;;;This is a modifier applied to when calculating whether to take captives or not for a particular unit. Depending on the units base morale this is either added or deducted from the chance to take captives:::::autoresolve_base_ratio_of_captives;;;;;Base ratio of captives to take in the range 0.0 -> 1.0. This is then modified. Keep to a low number.:::::autoresolve_base_ratio_of_captives_modifier;;;;;This is a modifier that\'s randomised and then added or subtracted from the base ratio. So If you have a base ratio of 0.1 (10%) and a modifier of 0.75 (75%) you will have a base ratio between 0.025 and 0.175.:::::autoresolve_chance_of_not_capturing_ship;;;;;(IN GAME) The chance we will not take a ship from the set of possible ships to capture:::::autoresolve_chance_of_taking_captives;;;;;Base chance ( 0.0 -> 1.0 ) of taking captives. Modified by generals, being out numbered etc...:::::autoresolve_commander_star_rating_impact;;;;;(IN GAME) The effect an advantage in the generals star rating has on the win chances, effects the overall win chance:::::autoresolve_easy_campaign_AI_percent_reduction;;;;;(IN GAME) The amount to increase AI casualties in autoresolved battles when campaign difficulty level is easy:::::autoresolve_easy_difficulty_human_advantage;;;;;(IN GAME) The advantage (applied to combat potential) human units recieve when the battle is austoresolved on battle difficulty easy:::::autoresolve_gaussian_boundary;;;;;(IN GAME) Represents a positive/negative range for Gaussian random numbers - number will never be out of this range:::::autoresolve_gaussian_standard_deviation;;;;;(IN GAME) The standard deviation to be used when calculating Gaussian random numbers:::::autoresolve_hard_campaign_AI_percent_increase;;;;;(IN GAME) The amount to decrease AI casulaties in autoresolved battles when campaign difficulty level is hard:::::autoresolve_hard_difficulty_AI_advantage;;;;;(IN GAME) The advantage (applied to combat potential) AI units recieve when the battle is autoresolved on battle difficulty hard:::::autoresolve_major_land_victory_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage improvement/impedance (winner/loser respectively) on a major victory:::::autoresolve_major_naval_victory_lose_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage impedance for naval loser on a major loss:::::autoresolve_major_naval_victory_win_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage improvement for naval winner on a major victory:::::autoresolve_min_combat_potential_only_win_chance;;;;;(IN GAME) The percentage of the win chances that should always be calculated by the unit combat potential alone.:::::autoresolve_minimum_casualties_on_lose;;;;;(IN GAME) The minimum casualties percentage for a unit on an alliances lose:::::autoresolve_minimum_casualties_on_win;;;;;(IN GAME) The minimum casualties percentage for a unit on an alliances win (altered for class and relative strengths):::::autoresolve_minimum_win_chance_to_win;;;;;(IN GAME) The minimum win chance of an alliance, if their win chance is less than this they cannot win the autoresolve battle.:::::autoresolve_minor_land_victory_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage improvement/impedance (loser/winner respectively) on a minor victory:::::autoresolve_minor_naval_victory_lose_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage impedance for naval loser on a minor loss:::::autoresolve_minor_naval_victory_win_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage improvement for naval winner on a minor victory:::::autoresolve_normal_naval_victory_lose_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage impedance for naval loser on a normal loss:::::autoresolve_normal_naval_victory_win_percent;;;;;(IN GAME) The casualty percentage improvement for naval winner on a normal victory:::::autoresolve_relative_captives_fuzziness;;;;;The randomness to apply to the amount of captives % of base captives - keep it low:::::autoresolve_ship_damage_capture_multiplier;;;;;(IN GAME) The percentage of damage to keep on a ship that has been reassigned from sunk to captured:::::autoresolve_ship_damage_fuzziness;;;;;(IN GAME) Randomness of each ships damage, to represent vageries of battle - keep it low:::::autoresolve_ship_damage_required_for_sink;;;;;(IN GAME) The percent damage required for a ship unit to sink:::::autoresolve_stat_massacre_chance;;;;;(IN GAME) Chance of massacre, compared to a normal win:::::autoresolve_unit_losses_fuzziness;;;;;(IN GAME) Randomness of each units losses, to represent vageries of battle - keep it low:::::autoresolve_unlikely_naval_result_scaling_factor;;;;;(IN GAME) The amount the damage probability should be scaled by the win chance in a naval battle with an unlikely result:::::autoresolve_very_hard_campaign_AI_percent_increase;;;;;(IN GAME) The amount to decrease AI casulaties in autoresolved battles when campaign difficulty level is very hard:::::autoresolve_very_hard_difficulty_AI_advantage;;;;;(IN GAME) The advantage (applied to combat potential) AI units recieve when the battle is austoresolved on battle difficulty very hard:::::background_commodity_supply;;;;;(IN GAME) Number of commodity units always available on the global market for each commodity (to prevent division by zero).:::::base_wealth_increase;;;;;(IN GAME) The base amount of TW required for a town to grow its wealth level. Formula: base_wealth_increase*power((total_wealth_increases+1),2):::::baseline_pop_growth;;;;;(IN GAME). Pop growth percentage in every region regardless of farms. We might want to define this on a per-region basis?:::::captured_required_region_prestige_multiplier;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only.The multiplier applied to a regions prestige if that region is a region the capturing faction must capture to fulfill its victory conditions:::::character_research_points_cap;;;;;(IN GAME)  Research points being contributed by character attributes are clamped to this value in any research slot:::::faction_gdp_other;;;;;(IN GAME) Background gdp value.:::::faction_gdp_other_minor;;;;;(IN GAME) Background gdp value for minor nations.:::::faction_leader_management_level_0_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_1_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_2_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_3_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_4_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_5_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_6_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_7_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_8_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_level_9_to_value;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. This maps the faction leaders management attribute to a value ( such as +1 / -1 etc... ). This is applied to the ministers management level for working out the minister effects.:::::faction_leader_management_value_mod_abs_monarchy;;;;;This is multiplied to the value for the faction_leader_management_level for an absolute monarchy government type.:::::faction_leader_management_value_mod_cons_monarchy;;;;;This is multiplied to the value for the faction_leader_management_level for a constitutional monarchy government type.:::::faction_leader_management_value_mod_republic;;;;;This is multiplied to the value for the faction_leader_management_level for a republic government type.:::::happiness_revolution_culture;;;;;?:::::happiness_revolution_neighbour;;;;;Happiness effect of revolution in a neighbouring faction (per faction).:::::happiness_war_drift;;;;;Happiness effect of revolution of any faction in the same culture (per faction).:::::happiness_war_lower_cap;;;;;Upper (positive) happiness cap for war-related effects.:::::happiness_war_major_defeat;;;;;Lower (negative) unhappiness cap for war-related effects.:::::happiness_war_major_victory;;;;;Per-turn drift towards 0 of war-related happiness effects.:::::happiness_war_region_conquered;;;;;Happiness effect of a major defeat.:::::happiness_war_region_lost;;;;;Happiness effect of a major victory.:::::happiness_war_upper_cap;;;;;Happiness effect of taking a region from the enemy.:::::immigration_capacity;;;;;(IN GAME). As percentage of population:::::losing_unit_minimum_strength;;;;;(IN GAME). The minimum pct of the losing units max soldiers a unit can have before it is destroyed:::::maximum_town_wealth_level;;;;;Levels of town wealth that exist in the game data.:::::migration_religion;;;;;0.0005 (IN GAME). Means X% of the minority will emigate:::::migration_unhappiness;;;;;0.012 (IN GAME). Percentage of net unhappiness contributing to unhappiness related migration. NUP% * X% * pop = emigration.:::::minimum_population;;;;;Minimum popluation for a region.:::::minimum_population_after_recruitment;;;;;(IN GAME) Mimimum population that must be left after recruitment;  so population must be at least this PLUS the recruitment population cost to enable recruitment.:::::policing_automated_cap;;;;;(IN GAME). Maximum effect of happiness due to automated policing.:::::policing_automated_cost_per_pop;;;;;(IN GAME). Policing_pips (sum of both classes) * sqrt(population) * policing_automated_cost_per_pop:::::policing_garrison_cap;;;;;(IN GAME). Cap on happiness from garrisoned units.:::::pop_growth_for_spawn;;;;;(IN GAME). The percentage of population growth required to spawn a new town, relative to the population of the last spawning.:::::recruitment_population_cost;;;;;(IN GAME) Number by which population is reduced for recruitment of a single unit:::::road_level_0_action_point_cost;;;;;(IN GAME). The action point cost to travel 1 unit distance on level zero (unupgraded) roads.:::::road_level_1_action_point_cost;;;;;(IN GAME). The action point cost to travel 1 unit distance on level one roads.:::::road_level_2_action_point_cost;;;;;(IN GAME). The action point cost to travel 1 unit distance on level two roads.:::::road_level_3_action_point_cost;;;;;(IN GAME). The action point cost to travel 1 unit distance on level three roads.:::::state_gift_multiplier_linear;;;;;(IN GAME) State gift diplomatic effect = (gift_value * state_gift_multiplier_linear) + (gift_value * gift_value * state_gift_multiplier_quadratic / root(combined_gdp)):::::state_gift_multiplier_quadratic;;;;;(IN GAME) State gift diplomatic effect = (gift_value * state_gift_multiplier_linear) + (gift_value * gift_value * state_gift_multiplier_quadratic / root(combined_gdp)):::::tax_efficiency_log_base;;;;;(IN GAME) The logarithm base for the formula used for calculating loss of tax income from having too many regions.:::::tax_efficiency_modifier;;;;;(IN GAME) A multiplier on the loss of tax income from having too many regions.:::::tax_efficiency_region_modifier;;;;;(DEPRECATED) The percentage reduction in tax for each region in a governorship beyond the tax_efficiency_regions_minimum.:::::tax_efficiency_regions_minimum;;;;;(IN GAME) The minimum number of regions before tax efficiency penalties apply.:::::tax_efficiency_total_regions;;;;;(IN GAME) The maximum number of regions for tax efficiency purposes.:::::tech_first_in_culture_prestige_multiplier;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. The multipler applied to a technology\'s prestige if the discovering in faction is the first faction in its culture to discover that technology:::::trade_commodity_unexported_gdp_proportion;;;;;(IN GAME) The proportion of commodity value which is added to the region gdp if the commodity is not shipped to the home region.:::::trade_route_internat_sea_length_limit;;;;;(IN GAME) Length limit on an international trade route.:::::trade_route_land_sea_bias;;;;;(IN GAME) How much land routes are preferred over sea routes (0.5 = sea routes twice as preferred).:::::trade_route_value_accumulator_proportion;;;;;(IN GAME) The proportion of the trade route value that gets accumulated each turn, \"time factor\".:::::trade_route_value_combined_gdp_proportion;;;;;(IN GAME) The proportion of the combined gdps of the two factions which contributes to the value of a trade route.:::::trade_ship_commodity_volume;;;;;(UNUSED) Volume of commodities a trade ship can export.:::::unilateral_diplomatic_gift_state_gift_proportion;;;;;(IN GAME) The proportion of the value of a state gift obtained for a unilateral diplomatic gift of equivalent raw value.:::::unit_first_in_culture_prestige_multiplier;;;;;(IN GAME). Integer only. The multipler applied to a unit\'s prestige if the recruiting in faction is the first faction in its culture to recruit a unit of that unit\'s class:::::unit_minimum_strength;;;;;(IN GAME). The minimum pct of the units max soldiers a unit can have before it is destroyed",
            },
        },
